    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d340">

                <pb facs="1395" n="1237" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1237"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Dudley to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Lima,
                            Peru</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-01-26"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">January 26, 1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1244.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of the department’s instruction No. 375, of the 27th ultimo, directing me, in
                    view of the offer of this Government to accord to American consular officers the
                    privileges afforded the most favored nation in the settlement of the estates of
                    deceased Americans, to request the Peruvian <pb facs="1396" n="1238"
                        xml:id="pg1238"/> foreign office to cause each of the local officials of
                    this country concerned to be instructed to notify the appropriate consul of any
                    death of an American that may occur within his jurisdiction. I inclose herewith
                    a copy of my note making the request.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Irving B. Dudley.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d340-a1.xml" xpointer="d340-a1"/>
            </div>
